.TH MINIOS-INSTALLER 1 "August 2026" "MiniOS Installer 3.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minios-installer \- Install MiniOS to disk from live session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minios-installer
.RI [ --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minios-installer
is a GTK3 graphical wizard for installing MiniOS from a live session to a
target disk. It supports modular live installations and conventional native
installations. The wizard detects native-install capability from the booted
image rather than its release number. Images without the required format-1 kernel
metadata and EFI architecture contract automatically use compatibility mode and
permit live installation only.
.PP
The installer creates and validates an explicit partition plan before any
destructive operation. Placement modes include erase-all, existing free space,
alongside a supported final partition, and native GUI manual partitioning.
.PP
Requires administrative privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show a short usage message and exit.
.SH WIZARD
The wizard configures installation mode, security, location, wired network,
keyboard, users, modules, storage placement, and boot layout before showing the
final summary. Previously visited pages can be revisited until installation
starts.
.SH PLACEMENT MODES
.TP
.B Erase all
Create a new partition table and destroy all data on the target disk.
.TP
.B Free space
Create MiniOS partitions in an existing unallocated region.
.TP
.B Alongside
Shrink an eligible unmounted final ext2, ext3, ext4, or NTFS partition and use
the released space. Unsupported or unsafe layouts are refused.
.TP
.B Manual
For native GUI installations only. Stage exact-sector create, delete, end-only
shrink, format, reuse, root, child mount-point, ESP, and swap assignments with
undo and reset. No destructive operation runs before final confirmation.
.SH SUPPORTED FILESYSTEMS
.TP
.B ext4
Recommended Linux filesystem for live and native installations.
.TP
.B ext2
Linux filesystem without journaling, supported for live and native installs.
.TP
.B btrfs
Linux filesystem supported for live and native installs.
.TP
.B FAT32
Live layout only; limited to files smaller than 4 GiB.
.TP
.B NTFS
Live layout only. Existing NTFS may also be shrunk for alongside placement.
.SH SECURITY AND NETWORK
Security profiles are convenient, balanced, and strict. Live mode defaults to
convenient; native mode defaults to balanced. SSH and XRDP exposure are selected
separately from the profile.
.PP
Network setup covers hostname and wired DHCP or static IPv4. Wi-Fi profiles are
not created or changed. Native static networking uses NetworkManager when
available and falls back to ifupdown.
.SH SESSION PERSISTENCE
Live installations support native directories, expandable DynFileFS storage,
fixed-size raw images, and encrypted LUKS images. Container modes use perchsize
and default to 4000 MiB. Raw and LUKS are limited to 4000 MiB on FAT32;
DynFileFS is not subject to that single-file limit.
.PP
LUKS is shown only when the running initrd advertises
.IR /run/initramfs/etc/minios-initramfs-crypt .
Before disk changes, every source initrd is checked for
.IR etc/minios-initramfs-crypt .
The initrd creates the per-session changes.luks file and prompts at boot; the
installer never handles the passphrase. This does not encrypt a native root.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/applications/minios-installer.desktop
.br
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.minios.installer.policy
.br
.I /usr/lib/minios-installer/
.SH NOTES
.PP
Only works from a MiniOS live session. The running live-media disk is excluded
from target selection. Erase-all destroys all data on the selected disk.
.PP
Required root space is calculated from selected module data, boot assets,
persistence, and 25 percent filesystem reserve. ESP and native swap space are
accounted for separately.
.PP
UEFI is supported on GPT and primary MBR. BIOS is supported only on primary
MBR; BIOS on GPT and extended/logical MBR layouts are unsupported. Manual mode
also rejects LVM, RAID, LUKS, and mapped or nested storage.
.PP
Command-line frontend:
.B minios-deploy
(see
.BR minios-deploy (1)).
.SH AUTHOR
crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>
.SH BUGS
